  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Assume that \\(x\\) is a positive real number. Which is equivalent to \\[\\sqrt[3]{x\\sqrt{x}}\\,?\\]",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(x^{\\frac{1}{6}}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(x^{\\frac{1}{4}}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(x^{\\frac{3}{8}}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(x^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(x\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2008-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(\\sqrt{x}=x^{\\frac{1}{2}},\\) we have \\(x\\sqrt{x}=x^{1}\\cdot x^{\\frac{1}{2}}=x^{\\frac{3}{2}}.\\)\n\nTaking the cube root multiplies the exponent by \\(\\tfrac13,\\) giving \\(\\left(x^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{3}}=x^{\\frac{1}{2}}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(\\sqrt{x}=x^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)",
        "Then \\(x\\sqrt{x}=x^{\\frac{3}{2}},\\) and the cube root divides the exponent by \\(3\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
